Assemble an imported preset in the right order

The import saved the new preset before it loaded the decoration settings
of the imported file. The stored preset therefore held the decoration
settings of the session. The import also gave the save an underscored
name, which no other path builds. The preset list therefore held a name
that a later lookup missed. The window background block assigned the new
file name before the copy, so the copy looked for a file that the archive
does not hold.

Copy the image files under the file name of the preset. Load every part
of the imported file, then save under the name that the user entered.
Assign the new image name after the copy, as the three other image blocks
do.

The change sits on the branch work/presets of the local tree, as commit 4 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

